        <body>
            <div xml:id="d256">

                <pb facs="0439" n="399" sameAs="frus:frus1865p1/pg399"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Hunter to Mr.
                        Adams</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1442.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-06-05"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 5, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> You will receive herewith, for your
                    information and guidance, two official copies of the order rescinding the
                    passport regulation of the 17th of December, 1864.******</p>
                <p>Credible reports reach us through the press, from which it appears that the
                    capitulation of the insurgents under Smith took place on the 25th ultimo.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. HUNTER, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d256-a1.xml" xpointer="d256-a1"/>
